{title: Spooky, Scary Skeletons}
{artist: Andrew Gold}
{key: Bm}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]Spooky, [F#7]scary [Bm]skeletons
Send [G]shivers [F#7]down your [Bm]spine
[G]Shrieking [F#7]skulls will [Bm]shock your soul
[G]Seal your [F#7]doom to[Bm]night

{comment: Verse 2}
[G]Spooky, [F#7]scary [Bm]skeletons
[G]Speak with [F#7]such a [Bm]screech
[G]You'll shake and [F#7]shudder in [Bm]surprise
When you [G]hear these [F#7]zombies [Bm]shriek

{comment: Bridge}
[D]We're sorry, [A]skeletons, you're [Bm]so misunder[Gm]stood
You [Em]only want to [Gm]socialize (but [Em]I don't think we [F#7]should)

{comment: Verse 3}
'Cause [G]spooky, [F#7]scary [Bm]skeletons
Shout [G]startling, [F#7]shrilly [Bm]screams
They'll [G]sneak from [F#7]their sar[Bm]cophagus
And [G]just won't [F#7]leave you [Bm]be

{comment: Bridge}
[D]Spirits super[A]natural are [Bm]shy, what's all the [Gm]fuss?
But [Em]bags of bones seem [Gm]so unsafe (it's [Em]semi-[F#7]serious)

{comment: Verse 4}
[G]Spooky, [F#7]scary [Bm]skeletons
[G]Are silly [F#7]all the [Bm]same
They'll [G]smile and [F#7]scrabble [Bm]slowly by
And [G]drive you [F#7]so in[Bm]sane

{comment: Verse 5}
[G]Sticks and stones will [F#7]break your [Bm]bones
They [G]seldom [F#7]let you [Bm]snooze
[G]Spooky, [F#7]scary [Bm]skeletons
[G]Will wake you [F#7]with a [Bm]boo!
